   "q_en": "<p>One-quarter of a circular pizza of radius 21 cm was removed from the whole pizza. What is the perimeter (in cm) of the remaining pizza? (Use &#960; =22/7)</p>",
   "q_hi": "21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2330;&#2380;&#2341;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2346;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#960; =22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)",
   "options_en": [
    "99",
    "141",
    "128",
    "131"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "99",
    "141",
    "128",
    "131"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "solution_en": "<p>We know that perimeter of a circle=2*&#960; *R </p><p>As pizza is circular</p><p>So perimeter of whole pizza= 2*22/7*21=132 cm</p><p>As one quarter was removed, so perimeter that was removed=132/4=33 cm</p><p>Three parts perimeter=132-33=99 cm</p><p>So total perimeter of remaining pizza=99+21+21 (as it will be 2*&#960; *r +2r)</p><p>= 141 cm.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>We know that perimeter of a circle=2*&#960; *R </p><p>As pizza is circular</p><p>So perimeter of whole pizza= 2*22/7*21=132 cm</p><p>As one quarter was removed, so perimeter that was removed=132/4=33 cm</p><p>Three parts perimeter=132-33=99 cm</p><p>So total perimeter of remaining pizza=99+21+21 (as it will be 2*&#960; *r +2r)</p><p>= 141 cm.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>",
