   "q_en": "<p>In a triangle ABC, length of the side AC is 4 cm more than 2 times the length of the side AB. Length of the side BC is 4 cm less than three times the length of the side AB. If the perimeter of triangle ABC is 60 cm, then its area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) is:</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AC &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 4 cm &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; BC &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AB &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 4 cm &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 60 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "150",
    "144",
    "100",
    "120"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "150",
    "144",
    "100",
    "120"
   ],
   "answer": 3,
   "solution_en": "<p>Let AB = x, BC = y, and AC = z</p><p>z = 2x + 4 ...... (1)</p><p>y = 3x  -  4 ........ (2)</p><p>x + y + z = 60 ....... (3)</p><p>From (1), (2), and (3):</p><p>x + (3x  -  4) + (2x + 4) = 60</p><p>6x = 60</p><p>x = 10</p><p>y = 26</p><p>z = 24</p><p>From the length of sides of the triangle we can find that the triangle is a right-angled triangle.</p><p>Area of the triangle = <img width=141 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19946/image083.png\"></p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>Let AB = x, BC = y, and AC = z</p><p>z = 2x + 4 ...... (1)</p><p>y = 3x  -  4 ........ (2)</p><p>x + y + z = 60 ....... (3)</p><p>From (1), (2), and (3):</p><p>x + (3x  -  4) + (2x + 4) = 60</p><p>6x = 60</p><p>x = 10</p><p>y = 26</p><p>z = 24</p><p>From the length of sides of the triangle we can find that the triangle is a right-angled triangle.</p><p>Area of the triangle = <img width=141 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19946/image083.png\"></p>",
